Sorry, I was unclear; I meant that destroy armor could
affect anything, not that polytraps could. (And I was
thinking of the destroy armor spell, from Ls and
golden nagas and the like.)

You're quite right about polytraps. I suppose that the
decision of what to enchant may depend partly on
how soon you need the enchantment, and whether
you think the risk of losing it to a polytrap outweighs
the risk of finding a better item than the one you're
enchanting. My *guess* is that if you're early on
and you have a choice of
enchanting a shirt or a +0 pair of iron shoes, you'll
be more likely to get extra AC by enchanting the shirt
and then finding a + pair of shoes than you are to
lose the shirt by hitting a polytrap. But if I were you
I wouldn't take advice on that from the kind of guy
who accidentally overenchants his shirts (that would
be me).

Speaking of forgetting spoilers, Doug and Richard
are right that shirts are cheap. For some reason I'd
remembered them as pricey.


